+profile (assumed): herdr is a public, Apache-2.0 Rust terminal workspace manager (Cargo.toml v0.9.5, GitHub and Homebrew releases). This design is for a fork that adds resumable ssh sessions behind a kill switch (`HERDR_MOSH_RESUME=0`) with a small upstream footprint; the plain `SshStdioBridge` is the fallback for any unsupported path, so rollback is cheap. Users are developers; the data at stake is live terminal sessions and keystrokes relayed through a new long-lived keeper daemon on remote hosts, which may be shared multi-user machines. No money or persistent user data is involved; blast radius is moderate (likely few fork users, but a daemon and rendezvous socket on remote hosts, and the remote shell environment of every pane).
