+- [Should-fix] §Legs "Failure classification" (Remote-side failure bullet: "EOF before WELCOME, or no WELCOME within 8 s of HELLO (rule 6 'Silence')" → "On a reconnect leg it is Fatal"); rule 6 "Silence" / "Leg setup"; §Discovery "On a reconnect leg ... A remote-side failure there ... is Fatal"; Error handling (b) — On a reconnect leg, a link stall or EOF between HELLO and WELCOME is classed as a remote-side failure and therefore Fatal, ending a still-resumable session, while the same stall before HELLO or after WELCOME is Retryable. (new; introduced by the redesign-cycle-1 failure-classification amendment)
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Spec line 98 starts the 8 s silence clock when the local end writes HELLO, so WELCOME must arrive within 8 s. Line 168 puts "EOF before WELCOME, or no WELCOME within 8 s of HELLO" in the remote-side class; line 170 makes that class Fatal on a reconnect leg; line 172 and Error handling (b) (line 289) make Fatal end the session. A stall before HELLO is Retryable (line 100, line 164 "killed by its setup deadline"); a stall after WELCOME is "always Retryable, because the link died" (line 164). Only the HELLO-to-WELCOME window is Fatal. Reconnect legs carry ServerAlive 15x4 (attach.rs:1403-1419 via apply_noninteractive_ssh_options), and ConnectTimeout no longer applies once connected, so ssh does not exit 255 within 8 s of a stall; the bridge's own silence kill leaves a signal exit, which never reaches the ssh-level Retryable branch (line 166). The spec states no precedence between EOF-before-WELCOME and exit 255. The ready marker proves only that the remote shell started (attach.rs `posix_remote_output_command`, `printf` then `exec herdr`), not that the keeper is reachable. All three seats grepped the spec for tradeoff/accepted/flapping language and found none. Before cycle 1, Fatal covered only auth, host key and generation mismatch.
+  severity: Should-fix. The Blocking floor for "violation of the stated core purpose" was considered and not applied: the main resume path through an ssh drop or stall is intact, and the failure is confined to the one-RTT-plus-bring-up window of a reconnect leg. All three seats rated Should-fix.
+  fix-shape hint: on a reconnect leg, class pre-WELCOME silence or EOF as Retryable (within the give-up deadline); reserve Fatal for a positive remote signal (an explicit attacher/keeper END, or a non-255 exit the bridge did not cause); state the precedence between EOF-before-WELCOME and exit 255.
