+- [Should-fix] §Legs "Failure classification": "The ssh `Command` sets `LC_ALL=C`."; Key abstractions LegDialer Owns ("`LC_ALL=C`"); Unchanged behavior "Leg 0 uses exactly today's ssh options" — LC_ALL=C is set on the leg's ssh Command without leg scoping or forwarding suppression; with stock Debian/Ubuntu `SendEnv LANG LC_*` / `AcceptEnv LANG LC_*` it reaches the remote attacher, and a herdr server spawned via ensure_remote_server_running (and every pane shell) inherits the C locale for the server's lifetime, a regression versus upstream's plain bridge. (new; `LC_ALL=C` was added in cycle 1 to stabilise ssh stderr strings)
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Spec line 164 sets LC_ALL=C in the paragraph covering every leg that ends before WELCOME, leg 0 included; line 370 lists it as a general SshLegDialer-owned item outside the reconnect-only option list; line 172 says no stderr is read on leg 0, so leg 0 gains nothing from it. Line 153 and line 436 promise unchanged ssh options, not an unchanged process environment. External, fetched by the ground and reproduce seats: https://manpages.debian.org/bookworm/openssh-client/ssh_config.5.en.html states the Debian package sets `SendEnv LANG LC_*` in /etc/ssh/ssh_config (upstream default sends none); https://manpages.debian.org/bookworm/openssh-server/sshd_config.5.en.html states the package sets `AcceptEnv LANG LC_*`; `LC_*` matches `LC_ALL`. Repo: every leg's remote command runs host.rs `ensure_remote_server_running()` (host.rs:21, 39-61), which calls `spawn_server_daemon`; `build_server_daemon_command` (src/server/autodetect.rs:225-233) only redirects stdio and does not clear the environment; grep finds `LC_ALL` only at src/worktree.rs:327 and no `env_clear`. Saved machines do not pre-start the remote server (`connect_saved_ssh`, saved.rs:20-55), so leg 0 is often what starts it. Caveat narrowing impact: with managed config, `-F` makes ssh ignore /etc/ssh/ssh_config, so the leak then needs a user-level SendEnv or `manage_ssh_config=false`; it bites only when a leg is what first starts the server. The side claim that OpenSSH does not localise its messages was not verified by any seat and is not load-bearing.
+  fix-shape hint: scope `LC_ALL=C` to reconnect legs (the only legs that read stderr) and add `-o SendEnv=-LC_ALL` (OpenSSH 8.7+), or drop it and rely on the spec's exact match strings.
