+- [Should-fix] Local bridge behaviour > Session-end triggers ("Client EOF: the bridge sends END over the live leg..."; "SshStdioBridge drop or stop: the leg I/O thread polls should_stop every ≤100 ms and never blocks on the network"); Acceptance "Client exit ends its keeper session within 2 s when the leg is alive" — The spec does not say whether stopping the bridge sends END. On the normal `--remote` exit path, stop races client EOF, so the 2 s criterion cannot be relied on and a session the client has left can stay parked for the whole grace. (new) [lanes: completeness]
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Only the Client EOF trigger (line 142) sends END, "best effort". The drop/stop trigger (line 143) defines polling only; line 164 says a leg torn down for stop "is not classified"; line 367 says teardown "kills the child"; line 180 keeps Drop's semantics (stop flag, socket removal, join). Nothing says END is written or flushed before the kill, or that client EOF is checked before should_stop. Line 120 puts leg polling, timers and should_stop on one thread, so both events fall in the same ≤100 ms poll with no defined order. Repo (finding's citation; not re-read by the seats): run_remote's `run_client_process` (attach.rs:3577-3600) waits on the client child and `_bridge` drops at once (attach.rs:90-105); Drop sets should_stop and joins (attach.rs:3101-3120). If stop wins, the keeper sees leg EOF, parks the session (line 209) and holds the server connection for the 60 s grace (lines 218, 262, 437), still counted as an active client (D2). Acceptance line 320 demands 2 s for exactly this live-leg case; an e2e test of it would be flaky. Distinct from the iteration-1 rejection on the next-leg END: that rejection rested on the criterion being scoped to "when the leg is alive", which is the case this finding covers.
+  fix-shape hint: state that stop with a live leg writes and flushes END before teardown, or that client EOF takes priority over should_stop in the leg I/O loop; add the test.
