+- [Nit] §Discovery and fallback "The leg-0 rule" third bullet ("that one connection is served by upstream's plain bridge_connection with today's leg-0 options ... The next client connection tries resume again"); Acceptance "On leg 0, a keeper bring-up failure ... serves that connection through the plain bridge ... The client sees upstream behaviour." — The leg-0 plain fallback opens a second, independent ssh connection after the resume attempt has failed. For `--remote` users with interactive authentication and no ControlMaster that is a second password/OTP prompt; every fallback also pays the failed leg's bring-up (up to 5 s keeper wait or 8 s pre-WELCOME silence), and because no failure is remembered, a persistent host-side cause repeats that cost on every connection. "The client sees upstream behaviour" is overstated. (new; the leg-0 fallback is the cycle-1 fix for the iteration-1 Should-fix on fork-only leg-0 failures)
+  verdict: confirmed (reproduce ✓ / refute ✗-survived (refute seat REJECT, FYI) / ground ✓)
+  evidence: Line 153: leg 0 for `--remote` is "interactive with an inherited stderr, so password and host-key prompts still work". Line 156: the leg owns its ssh child. Line 185: the fallback is a fresh `bridge_connection` "with today's leg-0 options", so a second ssh child; "The next client connection tries resume again". Line 167 shows the spec knows re-prompting is a cost ("for `--remote` it would re-prompt") but never states it for this path. Persistent triggers include an unwritable or squatted rendezvous dir with a predictable `/tmp/herdr-mosh-<euid>` fallback path (line 192). Line 325 and line 413 claim upstream behaviour. Why Nit: the capability probe (§Discovery steps 2-3) routes incapable remotes to the plain bridge before leg 0, so this fires only on rare keeper bring-up faults; the connection still ends in a working session (outcome (c)); managed config with a ControlMaster avoids the second prompt. The refute seat's REJECT reads "upstream behaviour" as functional outcome only and notes the probe already costs an extra ssh invocation; the confirming seats accept that framing on impact and confirm only the unstated cost.
+  fix-shape hint: name the extra prompt and up-to-8 s delay as an accepted limitation in the leg-0 rule and acceptance text, or remember a leg-0 bring-up failure per bridge so later connections go straight to the plain bridge.
